{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>One of every offering.</b> One loaf of every kind is taken as the contribution for the priest who offers its service, and the remainder is eaten by the owners (Menachot 77a); and the meat belongs to the owners, apart from the breast and the thigh that are in it, as is explained below — the waving of the breast and the thigh in shelamim offerings — and the todah is called shelamim."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:19.882508176Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}